<!--
    kuna `loweredswitch tree`: a compare tree of more than sixteen cases.

    gcc -O0 lowers a sparse switch to a tree of `==` and `>` tests on the switch
    variable with no jump table, whatever its size.  loweredswitch finds the tree
    but takes three to sixteen cases only (the cap keeps a very wide synthesized
    switch away from the structurer), so this twenty-case switch stays a deep
    if/else tree.  `loweredswitch tree` moves the limits to two and sixty-four
    cases for a cascade that has a range node.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 "switch-model", option `loweredswitch on|tree`.

    gcc 15.3 -O0 -fno-pie -no-pie -nostartfiles -static -fcf-protection=none
    (x86-64) of

        __attribute__((noinline)) int sink(int x) { return x * 7 + 3; }
        int wide(int x) {
          switch (x) {
          case 3: return sink(1);    case 9: return sink(2);
          ...                        (cases 3, 9, 14, 22, 31, 40, 47, 55, 63, 71, 78, 86, 95, 101, 110, 118, 127, 133, 142, 150)
          case 150: return sink(20);
          default: return -1;
          }
        }

    Pass 1 is the default (`on`), pass 2 sets `loweredswitch tree`.
-->
